+## Requirement baseline trace
+
+- B1 (undo of a closed adopted tab brings back the original threads seat). Tier 3 drives the real graph daemon binary and real herdr-threads 3.6.0 through the production CLI (`herdr-graph undo --json`, plan apply): `undo_of_closed_adopted_tab_keeps_seat_and_external_membership`, `undo_of_closed_adopted_pane_keeps_seat`, `close_restart_then_undo_resurrects_the_seat`. Each asserts the same seat id on the reopened pane, no `threads_seat_history`, any bare seat minted during the undo retired, and the thread created outside graph still lists the seat. Composed-daemon sweep (`keyless_close_then_undo` x3) covers the three windows and the preview wording; tier 5 covers ResurrectSeat through `production_ports` in each window. Delivered at the test tier; the production code path itself is the src cluster's and seam reviewer's to trace.
+- B2 (frictionless Herdr restart). Tier 3: `keyless_cold_restart_without_session_returns_to_its_seat` asserts a `threads.rebind_held_seat` effect reaches Done and the seat is placed before any relaunched agent checks in, then a fresh start checks in onto the original seat; `cold_restart_brings_every_seat_kind_back` covers keyed, keyless-with-session and shell seats with both agents resumed by session, no `restart_held` row, no `rebind_refused` meta, nothing retired; `never_observed_keyless_clone_starts_after_restart` covers the hg-c9e never-observed keyless row; `late_rebind_binds_the_fresh_agent_at_its_next_prompt` covers threads down past the grace. None take an operator step.
+- B3 (v4 service session via upstream U1). Tier 5 builds graph's ports with `daemon::compose::production_ports` and calls `resurrect_seat` / `rebind_held_seat`, which only a v4 session can serve; pin fixture moves to 3.6.0 (`tests/test_isolation.rs`).
+- B4 (upstream U2 rebind of a restart-held seat). Tier 5 `rebind_places_a_restart_held_seat_on_its_pane` (Done, then `AlreadyResolved` on a second key) and tier 3 rebind-Done assertion above.
+- Trial finding 3 regression (spec 4.4): `undo_restored_agent_that_exits_is_relaunched_live` asserts the restore launch resumes `stub-1`, the exited restored agent is relaunched in the same pane exactly once over 10 s, and the seat stays put.
+
+## Review of the test changes
+
+- `support::agent_stub`: a shell `claude` that Herdr detects, runs the real threads Claude hook (SessionStart, and UserPromptSubmit on demand) against the rig's own state dir and socket, and optionally reports sessions to the rig's graph instance. It stays foreground until released; its processes carry the rig env and are reaped by `reap_root`. `freeze_at` SIGSTOPs the graph daemon; `E2e::drop` sends SIGCONT before SIGKILL, so a panic while frozen does not leak a stopped daemon.
+- `ThreadsDaemon` now owns copies of root, socket and env instead of borrowing `PrivateHerdr`, so tier 5 can restart Herdr under it; declaration order in every new test drops the daemon before the Herdr. `private_command` keeps `env_clear()` semantics.
+- `threads_bin::test_support_binary` builds the pinned threads with `--features test-support` into its own persistent `target/threads-bin-test-support` (one reused build dir, not per run), version-checked like the default binary.
+- `production_discovery_reaches_real_threads_daemon` now expects `Disconnected("graph-local: ...")` (hg-lnw.29) instead of `Rejected`; it still asserts a specific variant rather than any error, which matches the hg-lnw.24 namespace guard's intent (no register/dispatch against a fresh node).
+- Sweep `Window::Settled` asserts only that the externally sent pending invitation does not return; graph's own ordinary-invitation reset is covered at the unit tier (`src/threads/tests.rs` `resurrect_between_24h_and_7d_reissues_the_ordinary_invitation`, `resurrect_reset_leaves_other_rows_and_is_in_the_acknowledgement_write`, `operator_resurrect_ack_carries_the_reset`) and tier 5 shows threads mints episode 2 after 24 h.
+- `scripts/herdr-release-smoke` (not in this cluster, opened only to check the test-binary override): matrix mode filters `HG_*` except `HG_TEST_HERDR_BINARY` and `HG_TEST_THREADS_BINARY` and forbids nested Cargo, and its `threads_real` expected-test inventory is exact. At base the inventory already omitted `adopt_resolves_the_checked_in_seat`, so the matrix was already out of step; this branch adds five tier-5 tests whose `test_support_binary` returns the "matrix requires a prebuilt HG_TEST_THREADS_SUPPORT_BINARY" error in matrix mode, and four e2e tests not in its e2e list.
+
